From c2cdfccd768756b5dc6f5b892722a061da553d43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:39:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [AGS] FreeType: use the portable ANSI ftsystem.c under DJGPP,
 not unix

builds/unix/ftsystem.c (the "assume unix-y" else() branch's choice for
any non-Windows platform, DOS included) uses mmap()/PROT_READ/
MAP_PRIVATE for file I/O -- confirmed absent under DJGPP by
tests/probes/djgpp-runtime/ (mmap/mprotect symbols missing;
<sys/mman.h> exists but is a broken stub). Found build-testing patches
0001-0009: this is the first real source-compile failure once configure
succeeds, not a configure-time gap like Phase A's.

FreeType ships its own portable "ANSI-specific" implementation,
src/base/ftsystem.c -- plain stdio fopen/fread, no platform-specific
I/O API, already used by the WIN32 branch. Pairs it with the same
generic src/base/ftdebug.c the unix branch uses (not
builds/win32/ftdebug.c, which is Windows-specific).

Not in PATCH-SEQUENCE.md's original 22-patch sequence -- that document
only analyzed CMake-configure-time blockers, not source compilation.
Corrected in the same commit as this finding, per this repo's own
conventions (never silently).
---
 Common/libsrc/freetype-2.1.3/CMakeLists.txt | 21 +++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Common/libsrc/freetype-2.1.3/CMakeLists.txt b/Common/libsrc/freetype-2.1.3/CMakeLists.txt
index 7cefd7f27..5cb9fbcf8 100644
--- a/Common/libsrc/freetype-2.1.3/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Common/libsrc/freetype-2.1.3/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -42,14 +42,27 @@ target_sources(freetype
 )
 
 if (WIN32)
-    target_sources(freetype PRIVATE 
-        src/base/ftsystem.c 
+    target_sources(freetype PRIVATE
+        src/base/ftsystem.c
         builds/win32/ftdebug.c
     )
+elseif (DOS)
+    # DOS-PORT: builds/unix/ftsystem.c (the "assume unix-y" else() branch
+    # below) uses mmap()/PROT_READ/MAP_PRIVATE for file I/O, none of which
+    # DJGPP provides (confirmed absent by tests/probes/djgpp-runtime/;
+    # <sys/mman.h> exists but is a broken stub). src/base/ftsystem.c is
+    # FreeType's own portable "ANSI-specific" implementation -- plain
+    # stdio fopen/fread, no platform-specific I/O API -- used here instead,
+    # paired with the same generic src/base/ftdebug.c the unix branch uses
+    # (not builds/win32/ftdebug.c, which is Windows-specific).
+    target_sources(freetype PRIVATE
+        src/base/ftsystem.c
+        src/base/ftdebug.c
+    )
 else()
     # Currently assume all non-windows platforms are unix-y
-    target_sources(freetype PRIVATE 
-        builds/unix/ftsystem.c 
+    target_sources(freetype PRIVATE
+        builds/unix/ftsystem.c
         src/base/ftdebug.c
     )
 endif()
-- 
